# Angular — Black Armory UI

Target stack (intent; confirm when `package.json` lands): Angular standalone components, `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush`, Signals for local UI state.

## Required patterns

- **Standalone only** — no NgModules for feature UI.
- **OnPush everywhere** — inputs via `input()` / `input.required()`; outputs via `output()`.
- **Signals** — `signal`, `computed`, `effect` for component state; avoid dual Sources of Truth with RxJS.
- Prefer `inject()` over constructor DI for new code.
- Keep templates dumb: no heavy math in templates — push to workers (see `20-stat-worker.mdc`).

## UI bans

- No Material / Bootstrap / generic admin-dashboard chrome unless Brandin explicitly opts in.
- No nested scroll traps; one clear primary scroll region per view.
- No card-soup: cards only when they wrap a real interaction.
- No emoji as UI affordances; use icon system once chosen (TODO).
- Guest mode and status badges must remain readable without color alone (see `@docs/01-master-prd.md`).

## Structure (when scaffolding)

```
src/app/
  core/        # auth, API clients, guards
  shared/      # dumb UI primitives
  features/    # activity, loadout, vault, agent
```

Mark deviations in `progress.md`. Do not invent routes/services that contradict the PRD.
